From 758f2337a68a89d823b3dedce6bfb6d338422c08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:03:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): validate absent foreign dependency
 endpoints [daveey]

A partitioned live database deliberately omits foreign-origin tasks. Recovery
previously required both local endpoint rows before consulting authenticated
Board rows or the complete replica, so valid foreign links refused as missing.
Do not import tasks to satisfy this predicate: bind absent endpoint custody to
same-head authenticated evidence, immutable foreign origin, positive replica
version and validated containment context instead.

Snapshot replica rows/link/cursor/hold predicates transactionally, bind them to
the preview token and immutable receipt, and recheck after evidence and inside
the local apply/settlement transaction. Preserve local/canonical containment,
work/lease checks, exact rejected operations/history/tombstone, enrolled
identity, completed refresh/empty feed, reason/token CAS and 30-second budget.
No task, lifecycle, lease, dependency or canonical writes are authorized.

Proof: unchanged recovery 102 tests; foreign suite 31 tests; 44 consumer files,
1521 tests passed, zero failed. Whole-tree scripts/check: 21 checks, green.
Final acceptance test RED on original recovery: missing_endpoint; GREEN on
this source. Includes certified stop/release/renewal, provenance/version,
replica/head races, work/lease races and lifecycle/no-materialization assertions.
Operational recovery and deployed proof remain with t_eeeeee0000000021.
